    "why": "A note hits the kick and sets the floor its pitch falls to; a Trigger value hits it too and sets its volume (128 = 100 %, kept for later notes). Every hit becomes a kick on C2, its volume the velocity (Vel → level 50 %: velocity in proportion to the level); the song's most common note tunes the kick."
  },
  "unmapped": [
    {
      "param": "End",
      "why": "the pitch heads for End but falls past it to the note (Pitch limit), which tunes the kick; End shapes the fall, fitted at its default"
    },
    {
      "param": "T DecShape",
      "why": "the curve of the pitch fall: Neo Drums' is exponential; fitted at the default shape"
    },
    {
      "param": "B DecRate",
      "why": "the buzz layer's fade: Neo Drums' drive shapes the whole hit"
    },
    {
      "param": "C+P DecRate",
      "why": "the click's and punch's fade: Neo Drums' click lasts 15 ms, its sweep carries the punch"
    },
    {
      "param": "A DecSlope",
      "why": "the level's slope before the release: at its default it takes a sixth of the level; larger values shorten the kick, which the decay doesn't follow"
    },
    {
      "param": "NoteDelay",
      "why": "delays and retriggers within the row: Neo Drums' hits land on the row"
    }
  ],
  "tolerance": {
    "loudness_db": 3,
    "band_db": null,
    "from_hz": 30,
    "to_hz": 12000,
    "measured": "",
    "why_not": "Two different kick models: KickXP's pitch falls on a power curve with a buzz layer, Neo Drums' exponentially through a saturator. The pitch it ends on, the fall's time and the level are matched, not the spectrum band for band."
  },
  "remarks": [
    "Each KickXP track is a kick with its own settings; Neo Drums has one kick: the conversion takes track 1's settings.",
    "The sweep time is fitted at A1: KickXP's fall is quicker above it and slower below (at T DecRate 30, a time constant of 9 ms at A2 and 65 ms at A0).",
    "A Trigger value above 128 (louder than 100 %) plays at velocity 127."
  ],
